{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"submission_c42.json\",\"summary\":\"Review of the second-scenario direct check 46a5695874f2465da28c9cfcd03b2071 for unit-claim-client-future-shutdown-escape, preflight-validated with valid=True and no diagnostics.\\n\\nFresh execution e6a53d74753d4e2b880be03c0fe20b0d completed the comparison: the declarative prerequisite accepted matched, comparison_complete and witness_complete are true, and the assertion is violated — the future returned for an accepted VerifyLeader request reported responded_after_shutdown false and shutdown_escape false, so caller_can_complete was false, while the served control reported completed true. The gap is therefore not specific to Apply: VerifyLeader's request channel is buffered by the library itself, so the accepted-then-dropped shape applies without any extra configuration.\\n\\nProduct contents: the required checker_correspondence item (no_issue_found, empty counterevidence) covering requirement versus predicate, caller duties, identity/correlation, the event-based oracle, completion via non-blocking probes, and four limitations; an applicability item; and resolutions for the two open issues efdf1587f7ef4ee193a70f81ccc378fc (claim) and 1fd929e13106440db4d8e42ceafbc891 (harness legality), both disposing the Future.Error documentation condition as independent_scope with sources.\\n\\nExplicitly retained: the probe establishes the absence of a completion path from the future's state and cannot measure a hang; skipStartup replaces the running-node window; only Apply and VerifyLeader have been executed, with configurationChangeFuture, bootstrapFuture, userSnapshotFuture and leadershipTransferFuture unprobed (their unbuffered or single-slot channels narrow but do not remove the window); and whether completion after Shutdown is deliberately not guaranteed remains an open boundary.\\n\\nRun state: five in-scope findings with seven violated scenarios and two corroborating scenarios, correspondence no_issue_found on every scenario, and no pending review work beyond this product.\"}"}}
